    "result_text": "All 42 test classes pass (56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors), including the new `Cp42Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTimezone()` that maps the existing `getRegion()` result to its IANA name: `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`, and `null` otherwise. Reusing `getRegion()` keeps `timezone` consistent with `locality` (both flow from the same postcode-then-city region derivation).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` string property to the owner schema (after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(owner.getTimezone())\")` alongside the existing `locality` mapping.\n\nThe Cp42 acceptance test (`postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW \u2192 Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full suite stays green.",
